++# Agent Note: Runtime product-title contributions
++
++Status: proposed
++
++English | [中文](2026-10-12-runtime-product-title-contribution.zh.md)
++
++## Problem
++
++The browser title is `<session title> — <product title>`, and `DocumentTitle` writes it from two inputs: the selected Session's durable title, and a product title that only the build supplies. `AppFrame` resolves that product title once from `process.env.DSH_CLIENT_TITLE`, falling back to the localized `common.brand.localBuild` string ([ui-layout README](../../../../packages/client/ui-layout/README.md), [ui-brand-official README](../../../../packages/client/ui-brand-official/README.md)).
++
++A deployment whose brand is not the build's brand therefore cannot put its own name in the browser title. A brand plugin can occupy `sidebar.brand.name` and render any text, but the title is not a slot and carries no runtime contribution point, so the plugin's only route is a second writer racing `DocumentTitle` — a `sessions.list` subscription that rewrites `document.title` after React's effect, plus a `MutationObserver` to repair concurrent re-renders. Two writers of one document fact is the defect: whichever lands last wins, an extra render frame can flash the wrong title, and unmount ordering decides what the reader sees.
++
++## Proposal
++
++Provide `ctx.productTitle` from `ui-layout`, beside `ctx.layout`: a small registry of product-title contributions the frame's document title projects.
++
++- `ctx.productTitle.register(text, { priority })` contributes text and returns a disposer.
++- Contributions shadow by ascending priority, lowest wins, matching slot-cell shadowing; a second registration at an occupied priority throws at load.
++- `AppFrame` reads the winning contribution through the root entry's inject hooks compartment (`useProductTitle`), and folds back to `DSH_CLIENT_TITLE`, then `common.brand.localBuild`, while nothing registers.
++
++A brand plugin keeps its card and its sidebar occupant, and gains a runtime title route with no second writer. The registry rides the existing service and inject-hooks machinery; no new slot kind, no build step, and no change to the settings seam.
++
++## Alternatives considered
++
++**Extend the `sidebar.brand.name` slot to publish its text.** Rejected: a slot occupant renders a component tree, not a string, and the title must have a value even when the occupant renders an image or nothing.
++
++**Keep the plugin-side title writer as the only route.** Rejected: `DocumentTitle` remains the shell's declared writer, so a second writer keeps racing it, and the frame — not the plugin — owns the title's lifecycle (unmount restores the product title).
++
++**A `DSH_CLIENT_TITLE` runtime read.** Rejected: build-time environment literals are artifact content in client bundles; reading one at runtime does not make it configurable.
++
++**A `document.title` slot.** Rejected: slots render components, and the title is a document side effect whose consumer is the frame; a component-shaped contribution would have to render nothing and publish a string sideways.
++
++## Acceptance criteria
++
++- A plugin injecting `productTitle` and registering text changes `document.title` on the next commit, without subscribing to `sessions.list` or writing `document.title`.
++- With a Session selected the title stays `<session title> — <contributed text>`; with none it is the contributed text.
++- Disposing the registration restores the build-selected or localized product title.
++- `DSH_CLIENT_TITLE` and the localized fallback still govern deployments that register nothing.
++- Two registrations at one priority fail at load, naming the occupant; a lower priority shadows without an error.
++
++## Risks
++
++- A new client service widens the cross-plugin surface; the registry is deliberately small (read, subscribe, register) and its only consumer is the frame.
++- Contributions are not persisted settings; a brand that must survive reload has to re-register on boot, which is how every other client contribution behaves.
++- The bilingual pair and its pairing record are not written yet; `verify-translation-pairing` and `verify-agent-note-format` must pass before merge.
