+# Plugin patches (dsh-side)
+
+These patches are general-purpose harness changes this plugin needs for a documented capability that official extension points do not provide. Keep them rebased on the target harness tag; the plugin degrades without them (see each patch's report), so a missing patch is a reduced surface, not a broken plugin.
+
+| Patch | Capability | Report |
+|---|---|---|
+| `0001-runtime-product-title-contribution.patch` | Browser tab title uses the live configured brand (`document.title`), not only the build-time `DSH_CLIENT_TITLE` | [.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/runtime-product-title/report.md](../.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/runtime-product-title/report.md) |
+
+Apply from the harness checkout root:
+
+```sh
+git apply /path/to/plugin/patches/0001-runtime-product-title-contribution.patch
+```
+
+Verified against `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` (`packages/client/ui-layout` suite: 70 tests green; the patched package sources typecheck clean). Without the patch the plugin keeps its direct `document.title` writer, which races the shell's `DocumentTitle` effect and can flash the build title for a frame.
+
+Related request already on record: [deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness Discussion #7779 — "Let the brand occupant name the product in the window title"](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/7779) (0.1.5-rc.3, no replies), which reports the same fixed-product-title limitation and a `MutationObserver` workaround; the report's `ctx.productTitle` registry answers that ask generally. `deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness` has issues disabled, so Discussions is the request channel.
